  "raw_text": "No. “The current branch” identifies a movable branch state, not an immutable revision. The branch may have advanced, been rebased, force-pushed, or changed locally since the tests ran.\n\nTo conclude that the currently checked-out code passed, the record should include at least the tested commit SHA—plus any relevant uncommitted changes, test configuration, environment, and test command/results. Then verify that `HEAD` matches that SHA and the working tree is clean.",
